TITLE:: RERecorder
summary:: A named set of tracks recorded together, one Recorder per track, under a piece folder
categories:: Libraries>reCording
related:: Guides/reCording, Classes/REReplay, Classes/RETake, Classes/RCSong

DESCRIPTION::
Records several buses at once into stamped files code::<root>/<subfolder>/<stamp>_<name>[ <version>].<format>:: (link::Classes/RETake#*path::). A track's bus is a link::Classes/Bus::, a link::Classes/NodeProxy:: (its bus, read at record time: a chain stage can be cued before it is built) or an integer index.

code::prepare:: needs a running server: it makes the folder and one link::Classes/Recorder:: per track with stamped paths. code::start:: is quantized on a clock (the song's, once registered with link::Classes/RCSong#-addRecorder::); an unprepared recorder is prepared on the spot with a warning (unquantized). code::stop:: closes the files; the next start needs a new code::prepare:: (a new stamp). code::stopAfter:: counts seconds on SystemClock, whatever the tempo.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: server
argument:: root
argument:: subfolder
argument:: version
argument:: format
File format ("aiff", "wav").
argument:: numChannels
Default channel count for tracks whose bus has none (an index).
argument:: clock
argument:: node
The node the record synths are placed after (nil: the tail of the root node, after every group).
argument:: sampleFormat

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: addTrack
argument:: name
argument:: bus
argument:: numChannels
Chainable; re-adding a name replaces its track.
METHOD:: removeTrack
argument:: name
METHOD:: trackNames
METHOD:: tracks
METHOD:: pathFor
argument:: name
argument:: stamp
The file a track would get (pure).

METHOD:: prepare
argument:: stamp
METHOD:: start
argument:: quant
argument:: clock
argument:: node
argument:: alignToLatency
Delay the record synths by code::server.latency::, in line with scheduled bundles (conversion takes).
METHOD:: stop
METHOD:: stopAfter
argument:: seconds
METHOD:: isRecording
METHOD:: isPrepared
METHOD:: paths
METHOD:: stamp
METHOD:: clock
METHOD:: node
METHOD:: free

EXAMPLES::

code::
(
~song.addRecorder(\ambix,
	RERecorder(s, "~/piece/RecorderSC".standardizePath, "LeafHues/AmbiX", "w1", numChannels: 16)
		.addTrack('AmbiX Out', ~song.ambi.decoder)
).prepare;
)
~song.recorder(\ambix).start([4, 0]);
~song.recorder(\ambix).stop;
::
